  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "ZKIQ+W2ZX26jluk+kuokqa4tjzI=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:49:09.893Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "v6.0.0's breaking changes are short and each one is mechanical:\n\n**Node.js 24 is the minimum.**\n\n```bash\nnode --version          # must be >= 24.0.0\nnvm install 24 && nvm use 24\n```\n\nThis is also the floor the monorepo's own `engines.node` declares, so it applies to contributors and consumers alike.\n\n**`DriveEditor` renamed** \u2014 a bulk rename applied across all packages; search for old `DriveEditor` references and follow TypeScript's errors.\n\n**Delete generated subgraph code** \u2014 `rm -rf src/subgraphs/`, because subgraphs are now generated and loaded at runtime and a stale directory conflicts.\n\nWorth pairing with the breaking-changes guide's rule that breaking changes ship only in a major version after a 3\u20136 month deprecation: these three arrived in `x.0.0`, which is exactly where the process puts them. The Node bump is the kind that cannot be deprecated gradually \u2014 a runtime floor is a cliff \u2014 which is why it is announced with the command to check and the command to fix.\n\n## Provenance\n- `apps/academy/docs/academy/ReleaseNotes/index.md` \u2014 v6.0.0 \u203a \u26a0\ufe0f Breaking Changes\n\n_Extracted from the Powerhouse repository at **v6.2.2-dev.74**._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-03T07:49:09.893Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:49:09.893Z"
    }
  },
